(notes "Buffet: All You Can Sheet. The front office is open, though not yet for business: the game opens on the Portfolio, the day and four stocks on it, each its price and its change since yesterday, a market day a second, with the fine print at its foot. Behind it, the back office: the market's calendar; its dice, rolled once a day where anyone can watch them roll; the market itself, four waves and a drift; four stocks priced off it in whole cents, the dearest paying a dividend four days a year; the fine print, a disclosure a month; the Series 777's question bank, twenty questions awaiting an exam the regulator has yet to schedule; and the model's caveats, the things this game gets wrong, each with Management's response. Pick the Day, the Dice, the Market or the Stocks sheet to watch the model work, or the Caveats sheet to read, or the Disclosures or the Questions sheet among the hidden sheets.")
